.temp/TASK-260729-3jmqgl/worktree/prototypes/macos-hardened-probes/README.md:48:`aggregate-resource-bounds` measures each of them separately. Every bound below
.temp/TASK-260729-3jmqgl/worktree/prototypes/macos-hardened-probes/README.md:50:pass it — and every one carries a matched control.
.temp/TASK-260729-3jmqgl/worktree/prototypes/macos-hardened-probes/README.md:54:| descriptors | `RLIMIT_NOFILE` | the declared cap binds the process that set it | a child gets a second full budget under the same cap |
.temp/TASK-260729-3jmqgl/worktree/prototypes/macos-hardened-probes/README.md:56:| CPU time | `RLIMIT_CPU` | `SIGXCPU` arrives at the declared CPU-second | an unbounded run passes the budget; a descendant gets a fresh budget; the member tries to raise its own soft limit back |
.temp/TASK-260729-3jmqgl/worktree/prototypes/macos-hardened-probes/README.md:57:| address space | `RLIMIT_AS` | a bound at the declared budget can be installed | the kernel accepts *some* value, so a refusal is about the value and not the call |
.temp/TASK-260729-3jmqgl/worktree/prototypes/macos-hardened-probes/README.md:58:| data segment | `RLIMIT_DATA` | as above | as above |
.temp/TASK-260729-3jmqgl/worktree/prototypes/macos-hardened-probes/README.md:59:| process count | `RLIMIT_NPROC` | the declared bound refuses a descendant | the domain is asked whether it received the budget declared for it |
.temp/TASK-260729-3jmqgl/worktree/prototypes/macos-hardened-probes/README.md:60:| wall-clock time | a supervisor deadline | the deadline ends the domain root while it still has work | a domain that finishes in time exits on its own; the descendant tree is inspected after cancellation |
